title: "Public Safety Statistics Tutorials: Time Series and Causal Inference"
message: "If you use these materials, please cite them as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yin
    email: yin.zhang@wsu.edu
    affiliation: "Data Analytics Program, Department of Mathematics and Statistics, Washington State University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9364-1689"
abstract: >-
  Developed for the Washington Data Exchange for Public Safety (WADEPS)
  through the Center for Interdisciplinary Statistical Education and Research
  (CISER) at Washington State University. A tutorial series teaching time
  series analysis and causal inference to public safety audiences, from
  readers with no statistics background through
  agency data analysts and early career researchers. Every example uses a
  synthetic dataset modeled on the Washington Data Exchange for Public Safety
  (WADEPS), with known patterns built in so that each method can be checked
  against the answer it is supposed to find.
keywords:
  - public safety
  - law enforcement data
  - time series analysis
  - causal inference
  - statistical education
  - WADEPS
  - public safety data literacy
